# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Omikron reverse-engineering repo - what does NOT go in.
#
# Three reasons a path is listed here, and they are not interchangeable. Only
# the second is safe to relax:
#
#   (A) COPYRIGHT. Shipped game data, the disassembly of the game's binary,
#       and anything that reproduces either. This repository is public; the
#       game is not ours to redistribute. Bring your own - see README.md.
#   (B) GENERATED. Reproducible from what IS committed, by a command the
#       README names. Committing it only creates drift.
#   (C) JUNK. Scratch output, editor droppings, stale manual backups that git
#       history replaces.
#
# Every entry says which.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- (A) the shipped game -------------------------------------------------
# Your own copy of the disc, ~1.7 GB. INPUT ONLY: never written to, never
# committed. `fr/` is the name this tree used before 2026-09-03; kept here so
# an older checkout cannot commit it by accident.
/gamedata/
/fr/

# --- (A) the disassembly and everything mechanically derived from it -------
# `Runtime.exe.asm` / `.c` are an IDA listing of `Runtime 2.exe`, and a
# disassembly is a derivative work of the binary it came from. `clean/` is a
# mechanical pass over them (`_vmhandlers.json` is literally handler
# assembly), and `readable/src/*.c` is the hand-cleaned decompilation. All of
# it stays local. `tools/omkpaths.py` finds them wherever you keep them, and
# the 13 checks that read them skip cleanly when they are absent.
/Runtime.exe.asm
/Runtime.exe.c
/Runtime.exe.h
/clean/
/readable/src
/readable/types.h
/readable/decls.h
/readable/globals.h
/readable/runtime.h
/readable/libcode.json

# --- (A) extracted game assets and captures of the running game -----------
# `.DDM`/`.3DM`/`.ADP` and DIALOG are lifted straight out of the game.
/MORPH_ANALYSIS/

# renders of the game's own art
/renders/
/example_screenshots/

# --- (A) references read while working, kept locally ----------------------
# Read while working, never redistributed; `docs/` cites what was learned from
# each, which needs no copy here. CLAUDE.md 2's "not a source" table describes
# them.
#
#   adp/   vgmstream's ADP reader (ISC). Nothing links it - this project's
#          decoder was transcribed independently from sub_483200, and having
#          the upstream beside it was the point.
#   3do/   the 3DO console version's format documentation, plus a reference
#          Unity importer. NO copyright or licence header in any of the .cs
#          files, so their terms are unknown - which is the same
#          "all rights reserved" problem as publishing with no LICENSE.
/adp/
/3do/

# NOTE: `traces/frames/*.png` are NOT excluded. They are the engine's own
# framebuffer, and they are the only oracle `engine: frame` and
# `engine: silhouette` have - excluding them turns those checks off for
# everyone. Sixteen 640x480 stills used as verification evidence is a
# different thing from redistributing the asset tree. Revisit if that reading
# ever looks wrong.

# --- (A/C) raw session transcripts ----------------------------------------
# 120 MB, and they quote decompiled code inline. The rendered `.md` digests
# are committed instead.
/transcript/*.jsonl

# --- (B) local configuration ----------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific paths. `omk.conf.example` is the template and IS committed.
/omk.conf

# --- (B) build output ------------------------------------------------------
/engine/build/
*.o
*.d
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- (C) stale manual backups - git history replaces these ----------------
/010926/
/270826_1719/
/290826/

# --- (C) scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
/log
/engine/142
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code's own working state, and it MUST be ignored rather than merely
# left untracked: `.claude/worktrees/` holds git WORKTREES - a git repository
# inside this one - so `git add -A` picks the directory up as an embedded-repo
# gitlink and quietly commits a pointer to a checkout nobody else can resolve.
# That happened on 2026-09-04 and had to be undone with a reset; it also swept
# another session's uncommitted work into the same commit.
.claude/
